Why "or later"
--------------

The copied material named below carries an explicit "version 2 or later"
grant, so this tree uses GPL-2.0-or-later rather than GPL-2.0-only:

- sqlmap's LICENSE at tag 1.4, and the same file on master, both fetched
  2026-11-06, say the program may be used under "the GNU General Public
  License as published by the Free Software Foundation; Version 2 (or later)".
  Copyright line at tag 1.4: "sqlmap is (C) 2006-2020 Bernardo Damele
  Assumpcao Guimaraes, Miroslav Stampar." The master copy of that file
  extends the same authors' stated years to 2006-2026. errors.xml itself has
  no copyright header.
- Wapiti source files fetched from master on 2026-11-06 say "either version 2
  of the License, or (at your option) any later version."

Wapiti's README says "GNU General Public License version 2 (the GPL)" and its
pyproject.toml classifier is "GNU General Public License v2 (GPLv2)", which
does not repeat the "or later" words. The source-file headers do. This
repository follows those headers and sqlmap's "Version 2 (or later)" wording.
That reading is not a determination that every Wapiti notice is consistent.

sqlmap-derived detection data
-----------------------------

protest/active/mod_sql.py, the DBMS_ERRORS list.

48 of the 64 regular expressions match sqlmap's data/xml/errors.xml at tag
1.4 exactly (https://github.com/sqlmapproject/sqlmap/blob/1.4/data/xml/errors.xml,
fetched 2026-11-06). That file contains this expression as one pattern:

    check the manual that (corresponds to|fits) your (MySQL|MariaDB) server version

The same combined expression is in sqlmap tags 1.0.11, 1.1.11, 1.2.11, 1.3,
1.3.11, and 1.4. It is not in tag 0.9. Tags 1.5.11, 1.6.12, 1.7.11, 1.8.12,
and master split MySQL and MariaDB into separate expressions. The exact
commit this list was taken from was not identified. No sqlmap source tree is
vendored here.

The other 16 expressions are not exact text from the 1.4 file. They are wider
alternations, extra phrases, or two ClickHouse expressions. sqlmap master has
a ClickHouse block, and its regexp is not the same string. Those 16 are still
shipped inside the sqlmap-derived list; this notice does not claim each one
was copied unchanged.

Copyright (C) 2006-2020 Bernardo Damele Assumpcao Guimaraes, Miroslav Stampar
for the expressions that match the 1.4 file, under that tag's GPL version 2
