Wapiti
------

Pro-Test is not a vendored copy of Wapiti. The package follows Wapiti's
architecture. docs/wapiti-analysis.md is the author's notes on the Wapiti
3.3.2 layout. Those notes are not Wapiti's manual and not Wapiti's code.
No Wapiti tarball is in this tree.

A line comparison against Wapiti master, fetched 2026-11-06, found shared
source lines, not just a shared idea:

- protest/active/mod_sql.py GENERIC_PATTERNS uses the same pattern strings and
  labels as pattern_to_injection in wapitiCore/attack/mod_sql.py. That file's
  header is Copyright (C) 2008-2023 Nicolas Surribas and Copyright (C)
  2021-2024 Cyberwatch, GPL version 2 or any later version. The file also
  points its own DBMS patterns at sqlmap's errors.xml. Current Wapiti splits
  the MySQL and MariaDB "check the manual" patterns; Pro-Test does not, so
  that combined expression is attributed to sqlmap above rather than to
  current Wapiti.
- protest/active/base.py shares a block of lines with wapitiCore/attack/attack.py
  (33 lines of at least 30 characters). That file's header is Copyright (C)
  2008-2023 Nicolas Surribas and Copyright (C) 2022-2024 Cyberwatch, same
  grant.
- protest/core/crawler.py shares lines with wapitiCore/net/explorer.py,
  including limit_parameter_occurrences. That file's header is Copyright (C)
  2026 Nicolas SURRIBAS and Copyright (C) 2024 Cyberwatch, same grant. The
  shared lines were not dated individually.
- protest/net/scope.py, protest/active/mod_file.py, protest/active/mod_exec.py,
  and protest/active/mod_xss.py each shared only a handful of lines.
  protest/app/cli.py did not.

Copyright in those shared lines stays with Nicolas Surribas (the headers also
spell the name Nicolas SURRIBAS) and Cyberwatch, under the GPL version 2 or
later grant written in the Wapiti files. Year ranges differ by file and are
quoted from the headers fetched that day.

